<Base title="About — Clement"><section class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">BEHIND THE NOTEBOOK</p><h1>Hello, I’m Clement.<br/><em>This is my working notebook.</em></h1></section><div class="about-grid"><div class="prose"><p>A place to collect technical explanations, explore small ideas in code, and give projects a home beyond a repository.</p><p>The emphasis is on showing the reasoning: what a model assumes, why a design works, and where an experiment stops being useful.</p><h2>A starting point</h2><p>The first articles are example technical notes. Signal Lab is a working educational demo, and the notebook itself is an open-source site. More personal project stories can be added as the collection grows.</p><h2>Colophon</h2><p>Built with Astro, Tailwind CSS, and Markdown/MDX. Typeset in Newsreader, Manrope, and IBM Plex Mono. Code is highlighted by Shiki, equations by KaTeX, and diagrams by Mermaid.</p><p>Static pages, locally served fonts, no analytics, and no tracking cookies. A little less noise; a little more room to think.</p></div><aside class="about-aside"><p class="eyebrow">ELSEWHERE</p><p><a href="https://github.com/poytaytoy">GitHub / poytaytoy ↗</a></p><p><a href="/rss.xml">Subscribe via RSS ↗</a></p><p class="eyebrow">THIS SPACE</p><p>Software & systems<br/>Embedded computing<br/>Mathematical thinking</p><p><a href="https://github.com/poytaytoy/poytaytoy.github.io">Source repository ↗</a></p></aside></div></Base>
